course: dictionary
lesson: 2346
title: Many meanings of cry
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word cry has more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one. «Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room after Chloe's plaits are pulled so hard she cries.» Here cries means tears come from her eyes, because she is hurt and sad.
explain: Cry can also mean to shout. «"Look out!" she cried» is not about tears. It means she said it loudly, as a warning. Ask yourself: is someone sad or hurt, or is someone calling out?
explain: Cry can be a noun too. A cry is a loud sound of pain, fear or calling, or the sound an animal or bird makes. Birds have calls and cries. The clues around the word show you which meaning fits.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence. If «she cried» means «she said loudly» and it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Cry (verb) means to have tears come from your eyes because you are sad, hurt, or very happy.
fact: Cry out means to shout or call loudly.
fact: A cry is a loud sound of pain, fear or calling, or the sound an animal or bird makes.
fact: A cry for help is a sign that someone needs help.
fact: Spelling: cry becomes cried, but crying keeps the y, because «criing» would put two i's together.
exercise: «Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room after Chloe's plaits are pulled so hard she cries.» What does cries mean here? | *Has tears coming from her eyes because she is hurt | Laughs and jumps about | Shouts very loudly at the nurse | Walks quickly to the door
exercise: «"Look out!" she cried.» What does cried mean here? | Felt very happy | Dropped her bag | Fell fast asleep | *Said loudly, as a warning
exercise: The last verse asks: «Who were the first to cry Nowell?» Nowell is a Christmas shout of joy. What does cry mean here? | *Shout or call loudly | Have tears in the eyes | Whisper quietly | Sleep softly
test: In «a cry for help», what does cry mean? | *A loud call that shows someone needs help | A kind of warm coat | A type of bird | A quiet song sung at bedtime
test: Which is the correct past tense of cry? | criyed | cryed | crie | *cried
exam: In «They laugh till they cry, and Lily starts a list of Aussie words.», what does cry mean? | Shout loudly at the top of their voices | Whisper a secret to each other | Walk around the room slowly | *Have tears come from their eyes because they are very happy
